# Class: co:PMD_0020004 (composition data item)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 co:PMD_0020004 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 co:PMD_0020004 "See editior note of composition to underatand the difference between composition and chemical composition data items.

To understand the difference between the composition and the composition data item, one has to understand the difference between SDCs and GDCs in BFO. A triple \"material entity has quality compsition\", conveys the fact such quality exists without telling us what are fractions of compounds in this material entity. A triple \"compostion is subject of composition data item\" conveys that there's an information about values of these fractions. Think of comosition data item as a pdf where the composition is documented."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 co:PMD_0020004 "PERSON: Philipp von Hartrott")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment co:PMD_0020004 "These portions of other matters do not have to be portions of specific chemical elements, i.e., atomic composition, but rather portions of other substances, such as nitric acid and water."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label co:PMD_0020004 "composition data item"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:altLabel co:PMD_0020004 "composition specification"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition co:PMD_0020004 "Bei einem Zusammensetzungsdatenelement handelt es sich um eine Informationsinhaltseinheit, die sich mit der Zusammensetzung einer materiellen Einheit befasst. Es verfügt über Bruchwertspezifikationen für Mitglieder, die Werte von Anteilen von Verbindungen angeben, die Teile der materiellen Einheit sind."@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition co:PMD_0020004 "Composition data entity is an information content entity that is about composition of a material enity. It has members fraction value specifications which specifiy values of propotions of compounds, which are parts of the material enity."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:example co:PMD_0020004 "Nitric acid solution has quality  composition, and  the composition data item is about this composition.The composition data item has members fraction specifications of nitric acid, e.g., 4 vol.%, and distilled water. These fraction specifications specify value of pure substances of nitric acid and distilled water, respectively. Furthermore, these fraction specifications specify values of relational qualities (volume) proportion of nitric acid and (volume) proportion of distilled water."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(co:PMD_0000060 co:PMD_0020004 "true"^^xsd:boolean)
SubClassOf(co:PMD_0020004 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:IAO_0000027 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:IAO_0000136 co:PMD_0025001)))
SubClassOf(co:PMD_0020004 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002351 co:PMD_0025997))

# Class: co:PMD_0020005 (porosity)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 co:PMD_0020005 "Subclasses need to express the normalization basis, e.g. cout per volume or count per mass or volume per volume ..."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 co:PMD_0020005 "PERSON: Philipp von Hartrott")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label co:PMD_0020005 "porosity"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition co:PMD_0020005 "itensive quality embodiying the fraction of the materials (enclosing) spatial region occupied by pores."@en)
SubClassOf(co:PMD_0020005 co:PMD_0020335)

# Class: co:PMD_0020022 (corrosion)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 co:PMD_0020022 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 co:PMD_0020022 "PERSON: Philipp von Hartrott")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment co:PMD_0020022 "Corrosion is typically of interest when the change of the material affects the objects ability to fulfill its function."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label co:PMD_0020022 "Korrosion"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label co:PMD_0020022 "corrosion"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition co:PMD_0020022 "Korrosion ist ein langsamer chemischer oder elektrochemischer Zersetzungsprozess eines Materials aufgrund seiner Wechselwirkung mit der Umgebung."@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition co:PMD_0020022 "corrosion is a slow chemical or electrochemical degradation process of a material entity due to its interaction with the surrounding environment."@en)
SubClassOf(co:PMD_0020022 obo:BFO_0000015)
SubClassOf(co:PMD_0020022 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(co:PMD_0025013 ObjectIntersectionOf(co:PMD_0000551 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000080 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:BFO_0000040 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000091 obo:BFO_0000016))))))

# Class: co:PMD_0020023 (OBSOLETE metallic grain structures)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 co:PMD_0020023 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 co:PMD_0020023 "PERSON: Philipp von Hartrott")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label co:PMD_0020023 "OBSOLETE metallic grain structures"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label co:PMD_0020023 "metallische Kornstrukturen"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated co:PMD_0020023 "true"^^xsd:boolean)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition co:PMD_0020023 "Bei der metallischen Kornstruktur handelt es sich um eine kategoriale Wertspezifikation, die den Wert der Qualität der metallischen Kornstruktur angibt. Es beschreibt die Morphologie polykristalliner metallischer Werkstoffe. Polykristalline metallische Materialien bilden ihre Kornstrukturen typischerweise als eine dieser Kategorien oder als Übergangs- oder Mischungszustand davon aus."@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition co:PMD_0020023 "The metallic grain structures is a categorical value specification that specifies value of the  metallic grain structure quality. It describes the morphology of polycrystalline metallic materials. Polycrystalline metallic materials will typically form their grain structures as one of those categories or a transition or mixture state of those."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(co:PMD_0000060 co:PMD_0020023 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

# Class: co:PMD_0020024 (Wasserstoffbindung)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 co:PMD_0020024 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 co:PMD_0020024 "PERSON: Philipp von Hartrott")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label co:PMD_0020024 "Wasserstoffbindung"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label co:PMD_0020024 "hydrogen bond"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition co:PMD_0020024 "A hydrogen bond is a bond that binds one molecule’s hydrogen atom with the electronegative atoms of another molecule."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition co:PMD_0020024 "Eine Wasserstoffbindung ist eine Bindung, die das Wasserstoffatom eines Moleküls mit den elektronegativen Atomen eines anderen Moleküls verbindet."@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:example co:PMD_0020024 "The bond that forms between liquid water molecules at one molecules hydrogen ends and the other molecules oxygen end."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(co:PMD_0000060 co:PMD_0020024 "true"^^xsd:boolean)
SubClassOf(co:PMD_0020024 co:PMD_0050000)

# Class: co:PMD_0020025 (obstacle role)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 co:PMD_0020025 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 co:PMD_0020025 "PERSON: Philipp von Hartrott")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment co:PMD_0020025 "asdfasdf")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label co:PMD_0020025 "Hindernisrolle"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label co:PMD_0020025 "obstacle role"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition co:PMD_0020025 "An obstacle role is a role of an independent continuant C that is realized in a motion process and indictes that C hinders the motion of a participant in the process."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition co:PMD_0020025 "Eine Hindernisrolle ist eine Rolle eines unabhängigen kontinuierlichen C, die in einem Bewegungsprozess realisiert wird und anzeigt, dass C die Bewegung eines Teilnehmers am Prozess behindert."@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:example co:PMD_0020025 "A precipitate or grain boundary may hinder the motion of a dislocation."@en)
SubClassOf(co:PMD_0020025 obo:BFO_0000017)
SubClassOf(co:PMD_0020025 co:PMD_0020254)
SubClassOf(co:PMD_0020025 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000054 co:PMD_0020245))
SubClassOf(co:PMD_0020025 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000081 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:BFO_0000004 ObjectComplementOf(obo:BFO_0000006))))

